   "he": "כְּבָר רְמָא נִיהֲלֵיהּ רַב שִׁימִי בַּר חִיָּיא לְרַב, וַאֲמַר לֵיהּ: שִׁימִי אֶת! אֶלָּא בְּשֶׁשִּׁדְרָתוֹ עֲקוּמָּה.",
   "en": "The Gemara responds: «Rav Shimi bar Ḥiyya already raised this contradiction to Rav,» his grandfather, «and» Rav «said to him:» Are «you» really «Shimi?» Rabbi Ḥanina ben Antigonus is not referring literally to someone with two backs and two spines, «but to» a person «whose spine is crooked,» causing it to appear as though he has two spines. Such a person can survive but is disqualified from performing the Temple service."
  }
